From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:02:23 +0200
Subject: clk: intel: grx500: do not free a regmap owned by syscon

grx500_clk_init() takes the CGU regmap from syscon_node_to_regmap() and
calls regmap_exit() on it if intel_clk_init() then fails. The regmap
belongs to syscon: it is registered on the global syscon_list keyed by
device_node and is never taken off it again, so freeing it leaves a
dangling entry that the next lookup of the CGU node hands out.

The blast radius here is small, and smaller than the same mistake in
leds-lgm-sso.c that the previous commit removes. This is an __init
CLK_OF_DECLARE path that runs once before any other consumer can ask
for the CGU, and intel_clk_init() only fails on -ENOMEM, so the freed
regmap is not reachable in practice today.

That is an argument for leaving it, not a good one. The pattern is
wrong wherever it appears, this tree is about to carry a patch removing
it from a driver we did not write, and shipping that while our own
driver does the same thing is not a position worth defending. There is
nothing to unwind on this path in any case: intel_clk_init() allocates
with devm and registers nothing before it can fail.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/clk/intel/clk-grx500.c b/drivers/clk/intel/clk-grx500.c
index bcce6660fbcc..6ae36e27dc71 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/intel/clk-grx500.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/intel/clk-grx500.c
@@ -163,10 +163,8 @@ static void __init grx500_clk_init(struct device_node *np)
 		return;
 
 	ctx = intel_clk_init(np, map, CLK_NR_CLKS);
-	if (IS_ERR(ctx)) {
-		regmap_exit(map);
+	if (IS_ERR(ctx))
 		return;
-	}
 
 	intel_clk_register_osc(ctx, grx500_osc_clks,
 			       ARRAY_SIZE(grx500_osc_clks));
